{"definition":"Bacterial infection of the renal parenchyma and collecting system.","id":"RDE2_000800","name":"pyelonephritis","node":"Diagnosis","status":"proposed","status_date":"2026-09-02","version":1}
{"definition":"Pyelonephritis in its acute phase: edema and tubular obstruction that produce the imaging manifestations below. A subtype rather than an acuity element because acute and chronic disease manifest differently (subtype-over-attribute rule, 2026-08-25 exchange).","id":"RDE2_000801","name":"acute pyelonephritis","node":"Diagnosis","status":"proposed","status_date":"2026-09-02","version":1}
{"definition":"Alternating linear bands of higher and lower attenuation radiating from the papilla to the cortex on contrast-enhanced CT, or the equivalent on MR, from tubular obstruction and interstitial edema.","entity_type":"finding","id":"RDE2_000802","name":"striated nephrogram","node":"FindingClass","note":"No RadLex concept; the nearest is spotted nephrogram (RID35573). Candidate for upstream proposal.","status":"proposed","status_date":"2026-09-02","version":1}
{"definition":"Increased attenuation with linear or hazy strands in the perirenal fat.","entity_type":"finding","id":"RDE2_000803","name":"perinephric fat stranding","node":"FindingClass","note":"No RadLex or SNOMED concept found. Candidate for upstream proposal.","status":"proposed","status_date":"2026-09-02","synonyms":[{"term":"perinephric stranding","type":"synonym"}],"version":1}
{"definition":"Renal length beyond the expected range for age and body size. An interpretation of the renal length binding, not a measurement of its own (03 §9).","entity_type":"finding","id":"RDE2_000804","name":"renal enlargement","node":"FindingClass","status":"proposed","status_date":"2026-09-02","synonyms":[{"term":"nephromegaly","type":"synonym"}],"version":1}
{"definition":"Gas within the renal parenchyma, as distinct from gas in the collecting system.","entity_type":"finding","id":"RDE2_000805","name":"renal parenchymal gas","node":"FindingClass","status":"proposed","status_date":"2026-09-02","version":1}
{"definition":"Focal cortical thinning with retraction of the overlying contour, typically over a blunted calyx.","entity_type":"finding","id":"RDE2_000806","name":"renal cortical scarring","node":"FindingClass","status":"proposed","status_date":"2026-09-02","version":1}
{"definition":"A focal abnormality of the renal parenchyma not yet characterized. The lesion pattern applied at the kidney: a positively reportable class, so an ordinary FindingClass rather than a grouping node.","entity_type":"finding","id":"RDE2_000807","name":"renal lesion","node":"FindingClass","status":"proposed","status_date":"2026-09-02","synonyms":[{"term":"renal mass","type":"synonym"}],"version":1}
{"definition":"Dilation of the renal collecting system.","entity_type":"finding","id":"RDE2_000808","name":"hydronephrosis","node":"FindingClass","status":"proposed","status_date":"2026-09-02","version":1}
{"definition":"A walled-off collection of pus within the renal parenchyma.","id":"RDE2_000809","name":"renal abscess","node":"Diagnosis","status":"proposed","status_date":"2026-09-02","version":1}
{"definition":"Pyelonephritis with established parenchymal damage from prior or recurrent infection.","id":"RDE2_000811","name":"chronic pyelonephritis","node":"Diagnosis","status":"proposed","status_date":"2026-09-02","version":1}
{"definition":"Necrotizing infection of the renal parenchyma by gas-forming organisms.","id":"RDE2_000812","name":"emphysematous pyelonephritis","node":"Diagnosis","status":"proposed","status_date":"2026-09-02","version":1}
{"definition":"Chronic granulomatous destruction of the renal parenchyma, usually with an obstructing staghorn calculus.","id":"RDE2_000813","name":"xanthogranulomatous pyelonephritis","node":"Diagnosis","status":"proposed","status_date":"2026-09-02","synonyms":[{"term":"XGP","type":"abbreviation"}],"version":1}
{"definition":"Any abnormality of the kidney. A negative-only node: reported as 'no renal abnormality' and never asserted in the positive; the closed-world negation sweep applies here.","id":"RDE2_000814","name":"renal abnormality","node":"Grouping","status":"proposed","version":1}
